      "content": "Proponents of this view often cite studies that measure group differences in IQ scores as primary evidence. They frequently emphasize heritability estimates from twin or adoption studies, interpreting genetic influence as proof of biological distinction between groups. Furthermore, they may point to specific genetic markers or putative genes linked to cognitive function to support a biological basis for these observed disparities. In their framing, these aggregate data points are presented as causal indicators, suggesting inherent, measurable differences.",
