      "content": "i see. so they basically frame it as a matter of biological fact rather than just social constructs. if i'm looking at the actual \"science\" they use, do they argue that these genetic differences are fixed or immutable across generations? like, are they claiming these cognitive hierarchies are a permanent feature of certain racial groups?",
