      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, a core aspect of that framing is the notion of relative fixity, suggesting that observed cognitive hierarchies are biologically ingrained and therefore permanent. They argue that genetic predispositions are stable traits that do not easily change across generations or through environmental shifts. This leads to the conclusion that these perceived cognitive differences are intrinsic and immutable features of certain racial groups. This \"fixed\" nature is central to how these theories maintain the perceived legitimacy of group distinctions.",
